      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "C# / .NET",
      "question": "Overloading vs overriding?",
      "answer": "One-line: Overloading changes parameters; overriding replaces inherited virtual behavior.\n\n Interview answer: Overloading is compile-time polymorphism, while overriding is runtime polymorphism.",
      "example": "🚪 Multiple entrances vs rebuilt room\n\n Same name + different parameters | Base → Derived",
