      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "C# / .NET",
      "question": "Liskov Substitution Principle?",
      "answer": "One-line: A subtype must preserve the expectations of its base contract.\n\n Interview answer: Replacing the base type with a subtype should not break behavior or invariants.",
      "example": "🔁 Replace without surprise\n\nBase Contract ⇄ Valid Subtype",
