      "question": "What is a process versus a thread?",
      "answer": "One-line: Threads share process memory, while processes have stronger isolation.\n\nInterview answer: A process owns address space and resources. Threads execute inside the process and share heap memory, so synchronization is required for mutable shared state.",
      "example": "🏢 Process is an office; 🧵 threads are workers inside it\n\nProcess → memory + resources | Thread → stack + scheduling path",
