      "id": "project-guide-b3fed0ebab278acaf5355d59",
      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "C# / .NET",
      "question": "What is the async state machine?",
      "answer": "One-line: The compiler rewrites async methods into a resumable state machine.\n\nInterview answer: Await captures continuation state, but it does not necessarily create a new thread. For I/O, control returns while the operation completes independently.",
      "example": "🎞️ Method pauses on await and resumes later\n\nBefore await → pending Task → continuation → next state",
