      "question": "Task.WhenAll versus Task.WhenAny?",
      "answer": "One-line: WhenAll gathers all results; WhenAny returns the first completed task.\n\nInterview answer: WhenAll preserves exceptions in AggregateException alternatives and still waits for every task. I use WhenAny for racing independent operations, then handle remaining work and cancellation explicitly.",
      "example": "🍽️ Serve when all dishes vs bell for first dish\n\nWhenAll = wait every task | WhenAny = wait first task\n\nvar tasks = urls.Select(url => client.GetStringAsync(url));\nstring[] pages = await Task.WhenAll(tasks);",
