      "question": "ArrayPool<T> versus allocating arrays?",
      "answer": "One-line: Pooling reuses buffers for allocation-heavy short-lived workloads.\n\nInterview answer: ArrayPool is useful for hot paths with measured allocation pressure. Returning arrays promptly and not retaining references are critical, and pooling may not suit every lifetime.",
