      "question": "Stack versus heap: what belongs where?",
      "answer": "One-line: The stack supports call execution; the heap stores managed object lifetimes.\n\nInterview answer: Modern C# optimizations such as stack allocation complicate simple rules. I focus on object lifetime, escape analysis, allocations, and actual runtime behavior rather than saying every value type is always on the stack.",
      "example": "📚 Stack for call frames; warehouse for managed objects\n\nValue/state on stack or in object | references point to heap objects",
