      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "System Design",
      "question": "Choose SQL, NoSQL, or both deliberately",
      "answer": "- Relational databases fit transactions, constraints, and joins across checkout records.\n\n- Key-value stores fit simple, high-volume key lookups and expiring data.\n\n- Document stores fit aggregate-shaped records with flexible nested fields.\n\n- Search engines fit text relevance and faceting; they are not the order ledger.\n\nStart with the least complex store that meets the access pattern and correctness needs. Polyglot persistence adds operational cost.",
      "example": "",
