      "topic": "REST APIs",
      "question": "Pagination, filtering, and abuse limits",
      "answer": "Bound page size, query length, sort choices, filter count, and response bytes. Cursor pagination should encode the stable sort position and relevant query context; validate/sign it and still enforce authorization.\n\nRate-limit by authenticated identity, IP/device signals, and expensive operation. Return 429 with a retry hint where appropriate; do not make a client retry sooner than the service can recover.",
