      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "System Design",
      "question": "Transactional Outbox",
      "answer": "What it solves\n\nPrevents a database update succeeding while its event is lost (or an event being published for a rolled-back update).\n\nIn the shop\n\nOrder Service commits the order and an outbox row in one local transaction. A publisher retries delivery; consumers deduplicate because delivery is typically at least once.",
