      "id": "project-guide-7bcd8e310905a252a4701a03",
      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "System Design",
      "question": "Cache-aside",
      "answer": "What it solves\n\nReduces repeated reads and latency for data that can tolerate a freshness window.\n\nIn the shop\n\nCatalog reads check a cache first and load from the catalog store on a miss. Use short TTLs or invalidation for price changes; never trust a cached stock count as the final reservation.",
      "example": "",
