      "topic": "System Design",
      "question": "Retry with backoff and jitter",
      "answer": "What it solves\n\nRecovers from transient timeouts without retry storms.\n\nIn the shop\n\nRetry a timed-out inventory request with bounded exponential backoff and jitter only when the operation is safe to repeat (or has an idempotency key).",
