      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "REST APIs",
      "concept": "HTTP method semantics",
      "question": "Why is implementing a purchase operation as GET a dangerous API contract?",
      "answer": "GET is intended for safe retrieval and can be prefetched, cached, crawled, or repeated without a user's explicit purchase action. Use an appropriate state-changing method and validate authorization and request integrity. Idempotency and safety are different: a DELETE can be idempotent while still changing state. Repeated requests need not produce identical status codes to be idempotent.",
      "example": "GET /products/73 -> read product information.\nPOST /orders -> request order creation with an idempotency strategy.\nNever create an order simply by loading a link.",
