      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "REST APIs",
      "concept": "Conditional updates",
      "question": "How can ETag and If-Match prevent one REST client from overwriting another's edit?",
      "answer": "Return a version-derived ETag and require the expected validator in If-Match for a protected update. Compare it atomically with the durable update, not only in application memory before writing. A failed precondition can return 412. ETags describe representations, so define their scope and do not assume an HTTP validator alone makes every multi-resource operation atomic.",
