      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "REST APIs",
      "concept": "Rate limits and retry behavior",
      "question": "What should a client do after an API returns 429 with Retry-After?",
      "answer": "Respect the advertised retry timing where applicable, use bounded backoff, and avoid sending the same retry burst from every client at once. A rate limit may apply per identity, tenant, endpoint, or shared capacity; document the scope. A server should enforce the intended limit across replicas when necessary rather than relying on an isolated per-process counter.",
