      "topic": "Angular",
      "concept": "Async subscriptions",
      "question": "How can an Angular template consume a stream without a manual subscription for each render?",
      "answer": "Use the async pipe when the template can own the subscription. It manages subscription changes and cleanup as the view lifecycle changes. Manual subscriptions are still appropriate for some side effects but need explicit lifecycle management. Avoid duplicating cold-stream subscriptions unintentionally when multiple template bindings would repeat an expensive request.",
      "example": "<ng-container *ngIf=\"profile$ | async as profile\">\n  <h2>{{ profile.displayName }}</h2>\n</ng-container>\n<!-- Choose the template syntax supported by the application's Angular version. -->",
