      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Angular",
      "concept": "Stable list identity",
      "question": "Why should an Angular list track a stable item key rather than only the current array position?",
      "answer": "Stable identity lets the framework associate an existing view with the same logical item during reorder, insertion, and removal. Position-based identity can attach local UI state to the wrong item after changes. Use unique stable keys and do not regenerate them on every render. Tracking improves reconciliation but does not make costly component logic or oversized lists free.",
      "example": "trackById(index: number, item: Product) { return item.id; }\n// Use this stable key with the list syntax supported by the app.",
