      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "JavaScript / TypeScript",
      "concept": "Promise coordination and cancellation",
      "question": "Does Promise.all rejecting cancel the other pending operations?",
      "answer": "No. Promise.all rejects when an input rejects, but other operations continue unless their underlying APIs are canceled separately. Use AbortController with APIs that support it when cancellation ownership is clear. Promise.allSettled can collect individual outcomes when partial results are useful. Starting many promises at once also needs a concurrency budget for large workloads.",
      "example": "const outcomes = await Promise.allSettled([loadCatalog(), loadPrices()]);\nfor (const outcome of outcomes) {\n  if (outcome.status === \"rejected\") reportFailure(outcome.reason);\n}",
