      "id": "kr7-interview-971fb6b9d6e98fd008b3c50d",
      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
      "concept": "Heap-based top K",
      "question": "How can you find the largest K values without fully sorting all N inputs?",
      "answer": "Maintain a min-heap of at most K candidates. Add values until it is full, then replace the smallest candidate when a larger value arrives. This uses O(N log K) processing and O(K) extra storage, with extra sorting if the final K must be ordered. Define behavior for duplicate values, K equals zero, and K greater than N.",
      "example": "foreach (int value in values) {\n    heap.Enqueue(value, value);\n    if (heap.Count > k) heap.Dequeue();\n}\n// With k >= 0, the retained elements are the largest k seen so far.",
