      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Responding to unknown questions",
      "question": "What is a strong interview response when you have not used a proposed technology in production?",
      "answer": "Say what you have and have not done, connect the problem to concepts you understand, and describe how you would validate the unfamiliar option. Clarify requirements instead of bluffing implementation details. An explicit assumption and a thoughtful verification plan are more credible than claiming experience or performance numbers you cannot substantiate.",
      "example": "\"I have not operated that broker in production. I would compare delivery guarantees, ordering scope, replay, and failure recovery against our requirements, then test a representative workload.\"",
