      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Mentoring and review",
      "question": "How would you review a junior developer's risky change without taking ownership away from them?",
      "answer": "Explain the concrete failure mode and affected contract, ask them to trace an example, and agree on a focused fix and verification. Distinguish blocking correctness concerns from optional style preferences. Offer context and pair when useful, but let them implement and explain the solution. Follow up on understanding rather than merely replacing their code with your own.",
      "example": "Feedback: \"Two callers can pass this existence check. What enforces uniqueness at commit?\"\nAgree on a database constraint, safe conflict handling, and a concurrent regression test.",
