      "concept": "Complexity contracts",
      "question": "Why distinguish worst-case, average-case, and amortized complexity in an interview answer?",
      "answer": "They describe different guarantees and assumptions. Average behavior depends on an input model; amortized analysis spreads cost across a sequence of operations without assuming random input. State space usage too, including recursion and auxiliary structures, and do not convert Big O into an exact runtime claim.",
