      "concept": "Hash collisions",
      "question": "Why can two different keys have the same hash without being considered equal?",
      "answer": "Hashing chooses a candidate bucket; equality distinguishes keys within the relevant lookup structure. A hash is not a unique identifier or a secure checksum. Correct lookup requires a stable compatible equality/hash contract, while collision behavior affects actual performance.",
