      "concept": "Two pointers",
      "question": "How would you find a pair summing to a target in a sorted array without an extra hash set?",
      "answer": "Start at both ends and compare the sum. Move the lower pointer when the sum is too small and the upper pointer when too large, using the sorted-order invariant. Handle overflow, duplicates, and whether indices or values are required. Sorting an unsorted input changes total cost and original indices.",
      "example": "While left < right, compare a[left] + a[right] with target.\nChoose movement from the monotonic sorted order.",
