      "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
      "concept": "Prefix sums",
      "question": "How can prefix sums answer many immutable range-sum queries efficiently?",
      "answer": "Precompute cumulative totals so a range sum becomes the difference of two prefixes. Define half-open boundaries and a sufficiently large numeric type. The simple static array approach does not make frequent updates cheap; dynamic queries may need another structure.",
