      "concept": "Monotonic stacks",
      "question": "Why can a monotonic stack solve next-greater-element queries in linear total work?",
      "answer": "Maintain candidates whose answers remain unresolved and pop those resolved by the current element. Each index is pushed and popped at most once, giving linear total stack operations. Define whether equal values count as greater and store indices when distances or positions matter.",
