      "concept": "Cycle detection",
      "question": "How do slow and fast pointers detect a cycle in a singly linked list?",
      "answer": "Advance one pointer by one link and the other by two. They eventually meet if reachable links cycle; otherwise the fast pointer reaches the end. Use identity, not equal payloads, to compare nodes. Explain empty and one-node cases and any later cycle-entry calculation separately.",
