      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Project deep dives",
      "question": "Which architecture details should you be ready to defend for a project on your resume?",
      "answer": "Explain the user problem, boundaries, data flow, identity, persistence, failure handling, deployment, and trade-offs you genuinely worked with. Clarify what another team owned. Interviewers can probe decisions and incidents, so memorizing service names without understanding the actual flow is weak preparation.",
