      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Ambiguous requirements",
      "question": "What would you do when asked to build an underspecified feature under time pressure?",
      "answer": "Clarify the smallest essential user outcome, identify risky assumptions, and agree on acceptance criteria. Separate reversible details from decisions that create durable data or security consequences. Deliver a bounded increment rather than silently inventing major behavior.",
