      "company": "Subject practice",
      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Estimation uncertainty",
      "question": "How can you give a useful estimate when an integration is unfamiliar?",
      "answer": "State assumptions, break work into known and uncertain parts, and identify a short validation step for the largest risk. Give an appropriate range or checkpoint rather than false precision. Update stakeholders when evidence changes rather than hiding slippage until the deadline.",
