      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Ownership beyond coding",
      "question": "How can you show ownership without claiming you personally did every part of a release?",
      "answer": "Explain how you clarified scope, coordinated dependencies, validated behavior, communicated risk, and followed outcomes within your role. Credit collaborators and state limitations. Ownership means ensuring responsibilities are addressed, not erasing other people's contributions.",
