      "topic": "Behavioral",
      "concept": "Interview readiness",
      "question": "How should you use a question bank without treating memorized answers as proof of readiness?",
      "answer": "Practise explaining concepts in your own words, writing and testing code, defending trade-offs, and discussing truthful project examples. Use unfamiliar follow-ups to find gaps. Interview expectations vary by role, level, and employer, so no finite FAQ count establishes a verified coverage percentage or guarantees selection.",
